Maven Power Moves: Build & Debug Like a Pro

We’ve all been there—running mvn clean install and staring at a wall of logs, trying to figure out what went wrong. 🤯

Here are a few game-changing Maven flags that save time (and sanity):

⚡ Faster Builds

mvn -T 4 clean install → run with multiple threads

mvn -DskipTests → skip tests when you just need the build

🔍 Debugging Made Simple

mvn -X → full debug logs (what’s Maven really doing?)

mvn -e → show stack traces for failures

mvn -q → quiet mode (focus only on errors)

mvn -Ddebug → run with debug enabled for specific plugins

🎯 Pro Tips

Use Maven profiles (-P profileName) to isolate environments

Combine flags smartly, e.g. mvn clean install -X -Pdev

Mastering these little switches means you spend less time digging in logs and more time shipping code. 🚢
